   "author": "Gregg Cisneros",
   "date": "2022-10-21T17:09:21",
   "content_html": "<p>Great article! It was an awesome day and I&#8217;m looking forward to next year!</p>\n"
  },
  {
   "id": 7,
   "parent": 0,
   "author": "Ed",
   "date": "2022-10-31T20:32:40",
   "content_html": "<p>What an experience. Thanks for sharing.</p>\n"
  },
  {
   "id": 9,
   "parent": 0,
   "author": "Animal",
   "date": "2022-11-22T08:33:02",
   "content_html": "<p>Sweet recap!  I like that I went by the name Adam throughout.  Ill keep the alias or I can just be refered to as Animal.  Either one will keep me under the radar.</p>\n"
  },
  {
   "id": 10,
   "parent": 0,
   "author": "Nathan",
   "date": "2022-11-22T15:29:15",
   "content_html": "<p>I loved the recap!  Glad I could be part of the story.  Those were some monster pulls you did!  Sorry I wasn&#8217;t able to hang with you after mile 50, my legs just couldn&#8217;t hold that pace for 90 more miles.  I had tried to hold off the Kid and Animal when I spotted them in the distance at mile 120 something, but it was futile.  After they caught me I had some shifting issues and lost their draft, and I was sure I wouldn&#8217;t place as they rode away from me.  But I&#8217;m not one for giving up, as you never know what might happen, so I just pushed as hard as my legs would allow and to my surprise I took 3rd due to the Kid taking a wrong turn.<br />\nImagining you flintstoning those turns paints quite the picture in my mind.  I don&#8217;t know how you managed it, but a well deserved win for you Matti!</p>\n"
  },
  {
   "id": 75,
   "parent": 0,
   "author": "Jake",
   "date": "2024-10-08T22:15:15",
   "content_html": "<p>Ran into this while googling Red Granite race stuff. You are a talented writer. I have done this race several times and I was enthralled and laughing, not just at the experience but by your telling of it. Thanks for the chuckles!</p>\n"
  }
